ion, attitude.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further education. Strengths: decision quality, reliability, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Weakness: communication, development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Strengths: adaptability, attention, problem solving, responsibility. Weakness: teamwork attitude, leadership.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has strong reliability, decision making, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress handling and conscientiousness but uncooperative. Candidate A has technical but organization issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication issues, because reliability and decision quality are critical. Crew atmosphere positive suggests cooperation. Egocentric and communication difficulty are concerns but maybe less than uncooperativeness of B.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate C.\n\nMake contribution: \"I think Candidate C is best because ...\". Use facts: 100% reliable, quick correct decisions, positive crew atmosphere. Acknowledge concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but weigh against others.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
